# eta_ion(E) for H2, digitized from figure 4 of Backx, Wight &
# Van der Wiel (1976), J. Phys. B 9, 315 (the SMOOTH CURVE, which
# is what their sec. 3.3(iv) adopts for f^(0)(H+ + H2+)).
# Source: references/Backx_1976_JPB.pdf p. 8, pdftoppm -r 600.
# Axis calibration on the tick marks; the dashed line the paper
# draws at eta = 1 reads 1.0033, which is the y-scale check.
# Reading error: sigma_eta = 0.0034, sigma_E = 0.109 eV.
# NOT RELIABLE below 16.5 eV (the curve is near-vertical there)
# nor over 57.0-63.5 eV (the trace follows an error-bar cap and
# is dropped).  Between 46 and 57 eV the HD inset covers the
# curve and only 6 columns survive.
# E[eV]   eta_ion   1-eta
#
# The RECOMMENDED source below 18 eV is not this trace but
# the inversion of Backx tables 1 and 2 (bx_table_inversion.py),
# which needs no figure reading at all:
#   E   eta_tab   1-eta_tab
#   15.0    0.040     0.960
#   15.5    0.375     0.625
#   16.0    0.742     0.258
#   16.5    0.902     0.098
#   17.0    0.953     0.047
#   17.5    1.002    -0.002
